This is `2*p_size + 2`. And `bigint_monty_redc` accesses `z` up to index `z_size - 1 = 2*p_size + 1`.

Now, in `Montgomery_Params::redc`:
```cpp
BigInt Montgomery_Params::redc(const BigInt& x) const
   {
   const size_t output_size = 2*m_p_words + 2;
   std::vector<word> ws(output_size);
   BigInt z = x;
   z.grow_to(output_size);
   bigint_monty_redc(z.mutable_data(), m_p.data(), m_p_words, m_p_dash, ws.data(), ws.size());
   ...
   }
```

`z.grow_to(output_size)` where `output_size = 2*m_p_words + 2`. And `bigint_monty_redc` needs `z_size = 2*(p_size+1) = 2*m_p_words + 2`. These match.

But the issue is in `grow_to`. Let me look at it one more time:

```cpp
void BigInt::grow_to(size_t n)
   {
   if(n > size())
      {
      if(n <= m_reg.capacity())
         m_reg.resize(m_reg.capacity());
      else
         m_reg.resize(round_up(n, 8));
      }
   }
```

The issue: `m_reg.resize(m_reg.capacity())`. If `m_reg.capacity()` is **less than n**, then resizing to capacity would give a size less than n. But the condition `n <= m_reg.capacity()` ensures this doesn't happen.

