In `pow_mod.cpp`:
```cpp
void fuzz(const uint8_t in[], size_t len)
   {
   static const size_t max_bits = 2048;

   if(len % 3 != 0)
      return;

   const size_t part_size = len / 3;

   if(part_size * 8 > max_bits)
      return;

   const Botan::BigInt g = Botan::BigInt::decode(in, part_size);
   const Botan::BigInt x = Botan::BigInt::decode(in + part_size, part_size);
   const Botan::BigInt p = Botan::BigInt::decode(in + 2*part_size, part_size);

   try
      {
      const Botan::BigInt ref = simple_power_mod(g, x, p);
      const Botan::BigInt z = Botan::power_mod(g, x, p);
      ...
      }
   catch(Botan::Exception& e) {}
   }
```

`Botan::power_mod(g, x, p)` calls `Power_Mod pow_mod(p)` which calls `set_modulus(p, hints, false)`. If `p` is odd, it creates a `Montgomery_Exponentiator`. Then `set_base(g)` and `set_exponent(x)` are called, and `execute()` is called.

In `Montgomery_Exponentiator::set_base`:
```cpp
void Montgomery_Exponentiator::set_base(const BigInt& base)
   {
   size_t window_bits = Power_Mod::window_bits(m_e.bits(), base.bits(), m_hints);
   m_monty = monty_precompute(m_monty_params, base, window_bits);
   }
```

In `Montgomery_Exponentation_State` constructor:
```cpp
Montgomery_Exponentation_State::Montgomery_Exponentation_State(...)
   {
   ...
   m_g.push_back(Montgomery_Int(m_params, m_params->R1(), false));
   m_g.push_back(Montgomery_Int(m_params, g));
   ...
   for(size_t i = 2; i != window_size; ++i)
      {
      m_g.push_back(monty_g * m_g[i - 1]);
      }
   ...
   }
```

`Montgomery_Int(m_params, g)` calls `m_params->mul(v % m_params->p(), m_params->R2())`. This calls `Montgomery_Params::mul`:

```cpp
BigInt Montgomery_Params::mul(const BigInt& x, const BigInt& y) const
   {
   const size_t output_size = 2*m_p_words + 2;
   std::vector<word> ws(output_size);
   BigInt z(BigInt::Positive, output_size);
   bigint_monty_mul(z, x, y,
                    m_p.data(), m_p_words, m_p_dash,
                    ws.data(), ws.size());
   ...
   }
```

`BigInt z(BigInt::Positive, output_size)` creates `z` with `m_reg.resize(round_up(output_size, 8))`. So `z.size() = round_up(output_size, 8) >= output_size`.

Then `bigint_monty_mul(z, x, y, ...)`:
```cpp
void bigint_monty_mul(BigInt& z, const BigInt& x, const BigInt& y,
                      const word p[], size_t p_size, word p_dash,
                      word ws[], size_t ws_size)
   {
   bigint_mul(z, x, y, ws, ws_size);
   bigint_monty_redc(z.mutable_data(), p, p_size, p_dash, ws, ws_size);
   }
```

`bigint_mul(z, x, y, ws, ws_size)` calls `bigint_mul(z.mutable_data(), z.size(), ...)`. `z.size() = round_up(output_size, 8) >= output_size = 2*m_p_words + 2`. So `z` has enough space for the multiplication.

Then `bigint_monty_redc(z.mutable_data(), p, p_size, p_dash, ws, ws_size)` needs `z_size = 2*(p_size+1) = 2*m_p_words + 2 = output_size`. And `z.size() = round_up(output_size, 8) >= output_size`. So `z` has enough space.

